From 5d12656ba88432b6c6618b8c31918c89165cacc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:37:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: name JSON fields as log tools expect

The first JSON format used short names (ts, msg, func) that log
shippers and stores do not recognize, so every pipeline needed a rename
step. The generic JSON profile now uses the common names: time (RFC
3339, microseconds, Z), level (lowercase), category, thread and message.

The source location is only included with -logsourcelocations, as a
"source" object {file, line, function}, and the function is its bare
name ("CConnman::DumpAddresses") rather than the compiler's full
signature with return and parameter types (BareFunctionName). mocktime,
continued and ratelimited are unchanged and follow the message.

(cherry picked from commit c2e4c1302abe4786cd93c53bcaae5bf22bb77763)

N3-Source-Commit: c2e4c1302abe4786cd93c53bcaae5bf22bb77763
N3-Source-Export: 0016
